Before the code, one important constraint, because it changes the wiring: deep-sleep wakeup (ext0/ext1) only works on RTC-capable GPIOs, and GPIO3 isn’t one. So the PIR has to go back on GPIO13, which is RTC-capable. That means I need to retract something. The GPIO13/SD-card conflict I kept pointing to was very likely a red herring. The real causes of your write failures were the /sdcard path bug and the card’s filesystem. With the SD card in 1-bit mode, GPIO13 is a common choice for PIR sensors on the ESP32-CAM. If you ever see SD errors that only happen while the PIR is active, tell me and we’ll revisit.
